# Carom — Single player (Solo)

Solo is one of the two ways to play Carom, reached from `SOLO` on the main menu
(`specs/ui.md`). It pits player one — the left paddle, controlled by the human —
against the AI on the right. Everything else is the shared game: the field and
obstacles (`specs/playfield.md`), the balls, serving, and physics
(`specs/balls.md`), and the scoring and match flow (`specs/ui.md`). Solo and
Versus (`specs/modes/versus.md`) are otherwise the same game and differ only in
who controls the right paddle — the AI here, a second human there.

Every figure below is exported from `src/constants.ts` under the name it is given
here.

## Controls

Keyboard only. The controls are registered engine actions on the `LAYOUT`
(`dual-vertical`) touch layout. Register exactly the eight names in `ACTIONS`, in
that order, each bound to the keys `BINDINGS` gives it:

| Action | Keys | Does |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `p1-up` | `KeyW` | Moves the human's (left) paddle up. |
| `p1-down` | `KeyS` | Moves the human's (left) paddle down. |
| `p2-up` | `ArrowUp` | Also moves it up: Solo has no player two. |
| `p2-down` | `ArrowDown` | Also moves it down: Solo has no player two. |
| `confirm` | `Enter`, `Space` | Accepts the selected menu item. |
| `back` | `Escape` | Goes back a screen. |
| `pause` | `KeyP`, `Escape` | Pauses at any time (the `paused` screen in `specs/ui.md`). |
| `mute` | `KeyM` | Toggles mute. |

- `W`/`S` and `Up`/`Down` therefore both move the human's paddle, which moves at
  `PADDLE_SPEED` while a movement action is held and is otherwise stationary
  (`specs/playfield.md`).
- `back` and `pause` share the `Escape` key. Read `pause` while a match is live
  and `back` on the menus, so `Escape` pauses in a match and goes back on a menu.

The right paddle is not player-controlled in Solo; the AI drives it (below).

## HUD

- The two scores sit near the top of the field in monospace digits `SCORE_FONT_PX`
  (`76`) tall, drawn in `COLOR.text`: player one's score centered on
  `x = SCORE_P1_X` (`520`) and player two's on `x = SCORE_P2_X` (`760`), with
  their tops at `y = SCORE_TOP_Y` (`40`).
- The mode label `MODE_LABEL.solo` (`SOLO`) sits small and dim, in
  `COLOR.textDim`, in the top-left of the field during a match.

## AI opponent

The AI controls the right paddle in Solo. It is a competent but beatable
opponent, not a perfect wall.

- The AI moves its paddle vertically at a maximum of `AI_SPEED` (`560`) px/s,
  deliberately slower than the human's `PADDLE_SPEED` (`720`), so a well-placed or
  well-curved shot can beat it.
- When the ball is moving toward the AI, it tracks the ball's `y`, reacting with
  the lag time constant `AI_REACT` (`0.12` s) and stopping when the paddle center
  is within `AI_DEADZONE` (`10`) px of the target. It does not account for spin
  curvature, so a curving shot can get past it.
- When the ball is moving away, the AI eases back toward `AI_HOME_Y` (`360`, the
  vertical center).

The AI must stay clearly beatable by a skilled player while remaining clearly
capable of punishing weak play.
